  "id": "locks/answers-past-the-reentry-budget-of-a-set-of-a-deleted-room-leave-no-record-in-the-room-created-again",
  "title": "The answers to a delivery set of a room deleted while the set runs, and created again under the same id before it ends, are refused as in a room gone, the one past the reentry budget included: no record of them is stored in the new room",
  "rules": [
    "§13.5 Delivery lanes across processes",
    "§10.1 step 14",
    "§5.1",
    "§8.2"
  ],
  "notes": "One process, `max_chain_depth` 2: the reentry budget is 20 passes. `held` is held at `held` in its delivery to `ws`, while the agent `ai` answers it with 21 events. The room is deleted and created again under the same id with `sms` and `ws` only. Once `held` is let go, the first 20 answers re-enter and find the room they were asked in gone; the 21st, past the budget, is not stored BLOCKED in the new room either: each is refused as in a room the store no longer holds. The new room's first message takes index 0. Indexes are read without lifecycle records. The refusals' framework events are left out: 21 alike, an unordered match of them is costly to fail.",
